    <name>
      <text>14.3 Perpendicular Bisector</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p></p><p>The point A has coordinates \( ({@aa@}, {@bb@}) \)</p><p>The point B has coordinates \( ({@cc@}, {@dd@}) \)<br></p><p><br></p><p>(a) Work out the coordinates of the midpoint of AB</p><p>([[input:ans1]], [[input:ans2]])&nbsp;&nbsp;[[validation:ans1]]&nbsp;[[validation:ans2]]</p><p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br></p><p><span id="docs-internal-guid-a715314e-7fff-c222-dd9d-8fb0402bb6fd"></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="">(b) Find the equation of the line that is the perpendicular bisector of AB</p><p></p><p>y = [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p><p>[[feedback:prt2]]<br></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
