        <truefeedback format="html">
          <text><![CDATA[<p>Here is a worked solution:<br></p><p><br></p><p>First calculate the gradient of the line AB using the formula:</p><p>\( m_{AB} = \frac{y_A - y_B}{x_A - x_B} \)</p><p>\( m_{AB} = \frac{({@bb@}) - ({@dd@})}{({@aa@}) - ({@cc@})} \)</p><p>\( m_{AB} = {@grad@} \)<br></p><p><br></p><p>Now find the gradient of the line perpendicular to AB:</p><p>\( m_P = -\frac{1}{m_{AB}} \)</p><p>\( m_P = {@-1/grad@}&nbsp;\)<br></p><p><br></p>
<p>Now find the line with gradient&nbsp;\( m_P \) passing through \( mid(AB) \) using the formula:</p>
<p> \( y = mx+c \)</p>
<p>We know the gradient:</p>
<p> \( y = {@-1/grad@}x+c \)</p>
<p>We can substitute the coordinates of the midpoint to find c:</p>
<p>\( {@(bb+dd)/2@}={@-1/grad@} \times {@(aa+cc)/2@}+c\)</p>
<p>\(c={@-1*(-1/grad)*(aa+cc)/2+(bb+dd)/2@}\)</p>
<p>So the equation is:</p>
<p> \( y = {@-1/grad@}x+{@-1*(-1/grad)*(aa+cc)/2+(bb+dd)/2@} \)</p>
<p><br></p>]]></text>
